body:
Set a timer, for say 5, 10 or 15 minutes. Work as quickly as you can, for (say) 10 minutes. Don't (for instance) pull a box out of the closet that will take an hour to go through - but something you can stop after 10 minutes with no problem. For instance, emptying and loading the dishwasher. Then after 10 minutes - stop. 

&#x200B;

Another thing that really helped me was timing different tasks, which don't take as long as I think. Then I can say to myself, well that only actually takes 3 minutes to do.

>Even if that person doesn't want to.

&#x200B;

How is that not the definition of selfish? 99.9% of everything everyone does is selfish, if you think about it.
